wasm jit: direct calls from JIT code to guest InternalCalls and P/Invokes (gex)

A wasm-JIT body reached an InternalCall or P/Invoke only through the residual
(call_interp -> interp_entry -> the managed-to-native wrapper in the
interpreter), ~490 ns a crossing in the browser, and an embedder's
scripting API can take ~220k such calls a second (13.2M interpreter-routed
icall residuals a minute in one profile). mono_wasm_jit_gex_native_site resolves the
guest target at compile time for identity-marshalled signatures, and the
residual site calls mono_wasm_jit_gex_native_call on the same scratch
layout instead: null check of this, GC-safe transition for foreign
InternalCalls and P/Invokes, SetLastError, the interruption checkpoint.
GEXMONO_WASM_JIT_NATIVE=0 turns it off. Counters: [wasm-jit gex-native].
Also MONO_WASM_JIT_STATS_TOPN sizes the stats top-N tables.

Tests: tests/unity-dotnet T.NativeDirect, CallBench icall legs.

